  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "hoover washer drier showing EO3 wont drain, ive done the filter its clean. H3DS4965DACE. pump just buzzes. do i need a new pump??"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "A buzzing sound usually means the pump motor is trying to run but can't turn. To confirm this: with the appliance unplugged and the filter removed, shine a torch into the opening and try to turn the plastic fan blades inside with your finger. If it is stiff, stuck, or you feel something blocking it, that suggests a jammed impeller (which might be fixable by clearing the debris). If it spins freely but still buzzes when running, the pump motor has likely failed and needs replacing."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "did that, power off. impeller spins totally freely, no resistance at all, feels like its not connected to anything. torch shows one fin looks snapped too"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drain pump (jammed or failed)]\nYes, you need a new drain pump. You will need to replace the drain pump unit."
  }
 ],
